<h2>What this replaces</h2>
<p>
    The usual Blazor data-fetching pattern is a <code>StateHasChanged()</code> after every await,
    which is both easy to forget and easy to overdo — the forgotten one leaves a stale screen, the
    extra one renders for nothing. Deja components call it never: state transitions drive rendering,
    and the deduplication above decides which of them are worth a pass.
</p>
